{"additions":753,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"Closes #182\n\n## What\n\nViews of a Projects board can now be defined in the config instead of saved on GitHub — a filter, grouping, sort, table columns and layout of your own, with no write access to the project.\n\n```kdl\nprojects-view \"Mine\" default=#true {\n    filter \"assignee:@me -status:Done\"\n    group-by \"Status\"\n    sort \"Target date\" \"asc\"\n}\n\nprojects-view \"Backlog\" {\n    layout \"table\"\n    filter \"status:Todo is:issue\"\n    fields \"Title\" \"Priority\" \"Assignees\"\n    board \"Roadmap\"\n}\n```\n\n- **`projects-view \"<name>\" { … }`** — top-level, repeatable. Children (all optional): `layout \"board\"|\"table\"|\"roadmap\"`, `filter \"<expr>\"` (the saved-view syntax, evaluated locally by `domain/filter.rs`), `columns \"<field>\"` (board columns), `group-by \"<field>\"` (swimlanes / table groups), `sort \"<field>\" \"asc\"|\"desc\"` (repeatable), `fields \"…\" …` (table columns), `board \"<title>\"` / `board <number>` (one linked project only). `default=#true` makes the board open on that view (at most one).\n- **Cycling** — local views follow the project's saved views in the `v` / `V` cycle; the header shows `<name> (local)`.\n- **Merge** — a same-named view in a later layer (user config, `.vig.kdl`) replaces it, other names are appended (`replace_named` in `merge.rs`).\n- **Unknown fields** — not a startup error: `⚠ view \"Mine\": no field \"Ghost\"` in the status bar, the setting is ignored for that board (`BoardPane::view_notice`).\n- **Refresh** — the shown view is now kept **by number** across a refresh of the same project (`applied_view`), so a change in the saved views can no longer shift the index onto another view (the local views are numbered from `1 << 40`, above GitHub's).\n- The cached / on-disk board stays as fetched; local views are appended only when the board is shown (`ProjectsState::show_board`).\n\n## Docs / demo\n\nConfig Reference (en / ja: table row, unknown-block list, new `projects-view` section with CI-verified examples), guide `views-projects` \"Local views\" section (en / ja), README key tables (en / ja), a commented example in `assets/default.kdl`. The Projects demo writes a config with a local view and starts vig with `--config`; the recording ends on `Open work (local)`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `projects_views_parse_and_validate` (loader: full form + 11 error cases), `projects_views_replace_by_name_else_append` (merge)\n- `local_views_join_the_saved_ones_and_a_default_one_opens_first` (state: scoping by `board`, `(local)` in the header, cache untouched, view kept across a refresh)\n- `a_local_default_view_opens_first_and_missing_fields_are_noticed` (board pane)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w\n","changedFiles":17,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-09T09:33:00Z","deletions":37,"headRefName":"feat/projects-local-views","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":183,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMxvE-w","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThere are a couple of small but concrete correctness/message issues (deduplication in unknown-field notices and inaccurate/awkward validation error text) that should be fixed before approval.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nAdds support for defining **local Projects views** (`projects-view`) in the KDL config so the Projects page can apply locally-defined filter/group/sort/layout/columns without creating or mutating saved views on GitHub.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Introduces `projects-view` parsing/validation and merge behavior (replace-by-name, else append) in the config layer.\n- Appends local views to fetched boards at display time, marks them `(local)` in the header, preserves the active view across refresh by view number, and reports unknown field references in the status bar.\n- Updates docs and the Projects demo tape/GIF to demonstrate `--config` with a local view.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| tape/demo-projects.tape | Writes a local config snippet and runs `vig --config …` to demo a local Projects view. |\r\n| src/projects/state.rs | Loads `projects-view` configs and appends them to a board when shown; adds tests for view ordering/default/refresh behavior. |\r\n| src/projects/panes/board.rs | Keeps view selection stable across refresh by view number; adds `(local)` detection and unknown-field notices; adds tests. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/types.rs | Extends `ProjectView` with `local` and `initial` flags; derives equality for `ViewSort`. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/graphql.rs | Initializes new `ProjectView` fields for GitHub-sourced views. |\r\n| src/core/ui/status_bar.rs | Shows `(local)` in the Projects header and renders `view_notice()` warnings in the status bar. |\r\n| src/core/config/mod.rs | Re-exports `ProjectsView`. |\r\n| src/core/config/merge.rs | Adds `projects-view` top-level merge behavior (replace named, else append) plus tests. |\r\n| src/core/config/loader.rs | Implements `ProjectsView` model, parsing/validation, and conversion to `ProjectView`, plus tests. |\r\n| README.md | Updates Projects keybinding description for `v` / `V` to include local views. |\r\n| docs/README.ja.md | Japanese README update for `v` / `V` local views wording. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/views-projects.md | Adds “Local views” documentation section. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/config-reference.md | Documents `projects-view` node and merge semantics with examples. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/views-projects.md | Japanese “Local views” documentation section. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/config-reference.md | Japanese `projects-view` reference section with examples. |\r\n| assets/demo-projects.gif | Re-recorded demo asset reflecting the updated tape. |\r\n| assets/default.kdl | Adds a commented example and description for `projects-view`. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (1)\n\n**src/core/config/loader.rs:753**\n* This error message says only `default=#true` is accepted, but the parser also accepts `default=#false` (and treats it as not-default). Update the message so it matches actual accepted values.\n```\n                    Some(other) => {\n                        return Err(invalid(format!(\n                            \"unknown property {other:?}; only default=#true is accepted\"\n                        )))\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 17/17 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 2\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-09-09T09:35:22Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"fc75808758435ef5d2cdfe59e42441b1179e09f6"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABM7l__Q","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-10T04:37:30Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"ca03fd9c2a605a962a0ff64c867ec83c069139f4"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABM7mCFQ","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-10T04:37:35Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"ca03fd9c2a605a962a0ff64c867ec83c069139f4"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABM7nVfw","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🔵 Needs a closer look\n\nConfig parsing/merging has a couple of verified edge-case inconsistencies (extra positional args silently accepted; merge key not trimmed) that can cause surprising behavior or validation failures.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (3)\n\n**Previously missed (3)** — in code that hasn't changed since the last review.\n\n**src/core/config/loader.rs:741**\n* `projects_views()` trims the view name for validation, but it doesn’t currently reject extra positional arguments after the name (they get silently ignored). This can hide config mistakes like `projects-view \"Mine\" \"oops\" { … }`; consider enforcing exactly one positional argument (the name) and treating any additional unnamed entries as an error.\n**src/core/config/loader.rs:826**\n* The `projects-view { sort ... }` parser currently accepts `sort \"Field\"` and defaults to ascending, but the documented/configured syntax is `sort \"<field>\" \"asc\"|\"desc\"`. Allowing the direction to be omitted makes misconfigurations harder to spot and diverges from the spec; require the direction explicitly.\n**src/core/config/merge.rs:80**\n* `replace_named()` matches on the raw first argument string. In `projects_views()` the name is `trim()`med before uniqueness checks, so a user override like `projects-view \"Mine\" …` vs `projects-view \"Mine \" …` won’t replace during merge and will later fail validation as a duplicate. Trimming in the merge key keeps merge behavior consistent with loader parsing.\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 17/17 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0 new\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-09-10T04:40:31Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"ca03fd9c2a605a962a0ff64c867ec83c069139f4"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-10T04:41:51Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34438176537/job/102747533156","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-09-10T04:41:57Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-10T04:39:58Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34437884066/job/102746656862","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-10T04:37:20Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-10T04:37:48Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34437884053/job/102746656601","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-09-10T04:37:20Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-10T04:38:29Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34437884066/job/102746656642","name":"build (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-24.04-arm)","startedAt":"2026-09-10T04:37:22Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-10T04:38:55Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34437884066/job/102746656833","name":"build (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-10T04:37:24Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-10T04:39:58Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34437884066/job/102747158140","name":"upload","startedAt":"2026-09-10T04:39:59Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-10T04:41:51Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34438176537/job/102747537771","name":"publish","startedAt":"2026-09-10T04:41:58Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-10T04:38:29Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34437884053/job/102746656467","name":"test (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-10T04:37:20Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-10T04:38:57Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34437884053/job/102746656625","name":"test (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-10T04:37:24Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-10T04:41:51Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34438176537/job/102747515901","name":"homebrew","startedAt":"2026-09-10T04:41:51Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"}],"title":"✨ Projects: local views from the config (projects-view)"}
